{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364130-is-target-number-manipulation-a-valid-mechanic-and-or-good-idea","id":1364130,"title":"Is target-number manipulation a valid mechanic and/or good idea?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-30T04:27:23-08:00","id":1364130,"title":"Is target-number manipulation a valid mechanic and/or good idea?","content":"I had an idea for artifact armor that makes the wearer harder to hit. Instead of 7s and higher counting as successes on a to-hit roll, only 8s and higher would count against the wearer. PEACH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T04:29:55-08:00","id":1364131,"title":"","content":"I mean that's always been the sidereal's shtick. <br /> <br /> How good an idea it is in their hands has been a subject of debate for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T04:36:25-08:00","id":1364134,"title":"","content":"We've already got every other sort of dice trick, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T05:15:58-08:00","id":1364136,"title":"","content":"Requires less re-rolling than other dice tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T05:23:01-08:00","id":1364137,"title":"","content":"Target number manipulation is very powerful, so you have to take that into account. In this case achieving the same to-hit chance against the armor wielder requires roughly 25% more dice than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T05:41:25-08:00","id":1364139,"title":"","content":"That is certainly true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T07:16:44-08:00","id":1364154,"title":"","content":"Efficiency of Charms that manipulate TN numbers is almost inevitably low at small pool size, high at high pool size, particularly if you have flat costs (and it's hard to have variable costs without introducing distorting &quot;cliff edges&quot; on costs and/or complexity in working out costs).<br /> <br /> That's not necessarily an irresolvable issue or bad, but certainly I think you'd have to totally design everything they can access around that assumption, and hand out a lot of Charms to balance out those strengths and weaknesses. It seems like the power / weakness of workhorse dice pools is essentially what each splat in Exalted has to have the rest of their Charms designed around, if they'll work at all (e.g. be more or less what the fiction says they should be).<br /> <br /> That's a bit of a problem if we like different varieties of Exalted who do/don't have TN manipulators to be able to draw on a shared set of artefacts / spells / MA charms as well! Maybe more of a problem than TN manipulators are worth, or maybe not.<br /> <br /> For your artefact, I'd guess it might be worth considering variable attunement and active costs depending on whether the character is of a splat with access to their own TN manipulators, so it's still *good* but not too good for characters with different native access. However since Sidereals aren't really written yet, and you're only balancing for you own game, I guess that's less of an issue than if you were writing it up as a canon artefact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T07:59:41-08:00","id":1364159,"title":"","content":"It's probably a bad idea for an Evocation without some restrictions on its usage, otherwise it will stack with things like Hail Shattering Practice, Gleaming Crescent Block and Blade-Deflecting Palm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T10:40:02-08:00","id":1364190,"title":"","content":"A concern that I haven't seen directly mentioned yet:<br /> <br /> Withering vs. Decisive.<br /> <br /> The game (at least attempts) to favor offense more on Withering attacks, and defense more on Decisive attacks. So written as a Withering- or Decisive-only or Dual effect would be much easier to get right than a Uniform effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T20:35:00-08:00","id":1364276,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of dice tricks personally, and I don't think they really line up with flavor very well. <br /> <br /> What specifically makes the wearer harder to hit? Evasiveness, thick armor, a forcefield? It would be better to make that an effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T21:25:57-08:00","id":1364281,"title":"","content":"I think TN manipulation is best done to one's self, and should be restricted to the Sidereal Charmset. It's just hard to remember as a player or a GM to count your dice differently because somebody asks you to (vs. counting your own dice differently based on your own effect). <br /> <br /> Stacking is my worry with non-Sidereal effects. You could say 'set TN to 6' instead of 'reduce TN by 1'. Also I think 2e said you couldn't go below 4's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T22:12:14-08:00","id":1364283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364130-is-target-number-manipulation-a-valid-mechanic-and-or-good-idea?p=1364159#post1364159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably a bad idea for an Evocation without some restrictions on its usage, otherwise it will stack with things like Hail Shattering Practice, Gleaming Crescent Block and Blade-Deflecting Palm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also clash with charms that reroll 6s. Eg Lightning Speed, Sensory Acute Prana, River Binding Wrath, Flawless Handiwork Method, Lore Inducing Concentration, Salty Dog Method, Knowing the Soul's Price, Unshakable Bloodhound Technique, Flying Steel Ruse, Four Glories Meditation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T22:37:10-08:00","id":1364285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364130-is-target-number-manipulation-a-valid-mechanic-and-or-good-idea#post1364130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for artifact armor that makes the wearer harder to hit. Instead of 7s and higher counting as successes on a to-hit roll, only 8s and higher would count against the wearer. PEACH.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really <i>really</i> depends on how much this costs, what else the thing does, and who's wearing it. <br /> Price this at 4m and hand it to Invincible Sword Princess and she just got a hell of a lot less vincible. <br /> Price this at 6m 1wp and hand it to Hot Hank, local DB brawler and it'll add some spice to a fight but not really change much. <br /> Price this at &quot;free, but only if you've already been attacked at least once this round&quot; and you've got a memorable duel-forcer for your boss-Sid while other folks fight with his underlings. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}